! New Delos Nexus ~ Region Worksheet

''The name rides the whole Nexus'' (ruled 2026-08-15): ''New Delos'' names the Aegean sea and
some of the coastlines surrounding it — all bordered by ''wild-magic seas and rift zones''. The
feeds' "New Delos" means this region, not one town; districts like the Spice Quarter belong to
the Nexus's fabric, and the ring-towns carry their own names (mostly still unwritten — see the
places shelf).

''Strata of one vertical Nexus.'' An Aegean low-sea archipelago of the Eastern Net — rocky
coastlines, olive-grove terraces, volcanic islands, crystal-clear harbors — with a flying capital
suspended over a megadungeon mouth, and beneath the mouth, the deep dark. Dream-mirror source:
Delos and Thira in an Ice Age low-sea period, pre-Hellenic sacred geographies overlaid.

''Timeline spine:'' YOLD 5002 — the Patroness stabilizes the Nexus, forces the arguing seas back
to the Apophis Datum, and ''lifts the old-empire New Delos complex on a gradient'' (the full
canon below); the craters left behind expose the megadungeon mouth. The same year she transmits
the ''Declaration of Confederation'', founding the League of Free Cities. Mana lifts near the
major Lares landmarks join the strata.

This worksheet grows by play; each stratum carries prompts beside its canon.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-neighborhood>>

!! The Neighborhood ~ grounding the concept map (Eastern Net, from the gazetteer)

''The Net's own words:'' the Eastern Net = "the heartland of Elyncia's surviving Nexus cluster,
bound together by tenuous ley-lines and centuries-old rivalries… coastlines gnawed by the Astral
Sea." Control of these Nexus = "the richest trade routes, the deepest dungeon mouths, the most
stable portals in the known world, and the few surviving corridors between them." New Delos sits
at the heart of it — ''central hub for League diplomacy'' — ringed by wild-magic seas and rift
zones.

''The compass of neighbors (for the image/concept map):''
* ''Neo-Thracia'' — the sibling across the unstable astral leg: mountain valleys, the Hebros
  river-gate, the lost Caverns; the campaign's destination; Lares recently reconnected after
  489 years, archive-nodes necro-script-corrupted.
* ''The Olympian Marches'' — the haunted corridor between Neo-Thracia and Illyria: broken
  mountains, divine weather, the Rift of Tempes, the Ash Plains of Phlegra strewn with giant
  bones — and the Gorgonne Diaspora among its named powers. The no-go radiance of the
  Gigantomachy's fallout lingers over the Heights.
* ''The Illyrian Archipelago'' — the ''sinking Illyria'' of Gaia's mythic history: the
  Western-Balkan Adriatic realm, its Montenegro-analog mountains half-drowned into volcanic
  isles — and ''the Necrospire impact crater sits among the Accursed Mountains'' (the
  Prokletije-mirror; full pattern at concepts/the-necrospire). Necro-cults at the crater, undead armadas, the old ley-hub toward the Western
  Net; the gazetteer's "off the coast near the mouth of Hebros" reads as the sea-route
  relation, not adjacency — the wound lies west across the Marches, the corridor between.
* ''The Summerlands'' — the breadbasket crossroads: Dominion south (Tharsis, the Prismatic
  University), Ouroborous warcamps in the haunted heart, Seelie kingdoms on the Faewild coast,
  Amaranth churches throughout.
* ''The Winterlands'' — the Lich's ground: the Imperator's Southern Marches feeding his armies
  through the Ironspine passes; the Shattered Crown of the old Winter Court.
* ''Asgard'' — the Bifrost transit hub joining Eastern and Western Nets; the World-Root Gate;
  the gods still face-to-face there.
* ''The Brimstone Mountains'' — the volcanic peninsula southwest: the Brimstone Court's caldera
  seat, Ashport's syndicates, the Hidden Crucibles, three rumored power cores.
* ''Beyond (Western Net):'' the Broken/Shattered Isles torn from Mu's shelf (Aki's home water) ·
  Mu · drifting Hawaiki · sealed Khemet · and the Verdant Coil shifting its astral position with
  its blooms, seller of the cedar that wards every iron-chest.

''The map's reading:'' New Delos = the calm eye of the Eastern Net — the stable center whose
neighbors carry the campaign (Neo-Thracia, north across the unstable leg), the wound (Illyria's
crater in the sinking Montenegro-analog mountains, west beyond the Marches), the war
(Summerlands/Winterlands), the forge (Brimstone), and the bridge out (Asgard).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-gradient>>

!! The Levitation Gradient

''The lift ran as a gradient, not a scoop.'' The old-empire New Delos complex — the island of
Delos and all the islands within roughly three 30-mile nexus-scale subhexes — rose by degrees:

* ''Delos itself rose entire'' — "mostly one piece," if you count the new sky bridges and
  stuckforce connections that stitch it — ''a small constellation'' rather than a single slab.
* ''Ninety percent of Rinia rose'' — and Rinia's departure from its bed exposed ''the dungeon
  mouth'': Low Delos opens where Rinia used to lie.
* ''Mykonos, Naxos, and the others rose by less, on a gradient outward'' — partial liftings,
  shorn heights, settlements suddenly airborne while their harbors stayed wet.
* ''Some chunks lifted from the seabed itself'' — ground that had never known air joined the sky.
* ''The gradient's far tail reached absurdly wide:'' it took holy sites and random cave-bearing
  crags as distant as the coast near the ''Temple of Poseidon'' in the Athens-region — and
  raised ''the whole six miles around the Temple of Artemis near Izmir'' as one piece. High
  Delos's constellation therefore holds ''far exclaves'': sky-fragments hanging over other
  coasts, joined to the capital by nothing but the DreamNet and the memory of the same morning.

''What the lift left below:'' the settlements that rose became ''skyports and sky-island hubs''
— so ''new towns and ports were founded at sea level after the flight'', young by Elyncia's
measure (490 years), ringing the crater-seas and the emptied harbors. The ring-towns carry their
own names; "New Delos" stays the Nexus's name entire. The old megacity went ''up''.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/high-delos>>

!! High Delos ~ the flying capital

''Canon:'' the Lindwyrm's capital and seat of the League of Free Cities — ''a small
constellation'': Delos risen near-whole, the partial heights of its sisters, and seabed-chunks
that never knew air, stitched by sky bridges and stuckforce connections. Cycladic marble footings
under Neo-Thracian brick under fae-grown coral — polyglot architecture on Delian designs, arched
walkways between raised neighborhoods, one bridge trussed with a repurposed trireme keel. The
levitated ''Theatre Quarter'' holds the wealthiest old houses, ''the House of Masks'' among them
(cabaret, maze-Inn, Order of Amaranth management — its own loci carry it). The ''Terrace of the
Lions'' gazes over open cloud; the round ''Sacred Lake'' rides the island; the ''Orrery of High
Delos'' turns somewhere near the summit of civic pride. The ''High Delos Archive'' seats the
Floating Librarians of Mu. Archive- and Market-Lares dominate the node traffic — and above them
all stands ''the Naxian Colossus'': the nine-meter archaic Apollo,
orichalcum-runed, ''the civic-scale ley-line node'' — the Temple-tier Lares anchoring High Delos
to the DreamNet, the great statue whose "stone eyes flared with inner light." A Naxian
dedication standing on risen Delos, while Naxos itself half-rose on the gradient — the givers'
island watches its gift from a lower sky.

''Prompts:'' which neighborhoods rose and which stayed? Who regulates the lift-queues? Where does
the Orrery actually sit, and who reads it?

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/low-delos>>

!! Low Delos ~ the megadungeon mouth

''Canon:'' where ''Rinia rose from its bed'' (nine-tenths of it airborne in the gradient), the
exposed crater opens a megadungeon ''piercing deep into the Underdark, with stabilized towns
down to the third level''. The crater-glow brightens and dims on
a nineteen-minute cycle that correlates with nothing and has outlasted four scholarly careers.
Scavenger-tier salvage economy; a "soulbound lash" of Rakshasa's anger came up from here.
Path-Lares maintain active Underdark maps. Mana lifts run between the ports of High and Low.

''Prompts:'' what do the three stabilized town-levels each trade? Who holds the lift-gates at the
bottom? What does the nineteen-minute cycle breathe FOR?

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/underdark>>

!! The Underdark ~ below the lowest layer

''Canon:'' Low Delos ranks among ''the deepest, most stable Nexus-to-Underdark routes'' in the
known world — a strategic fact the League guards. Underdark incursions number among the Nexus's
standing hazards; relic-hunting mercenaries destabilize dungeon floors. Past the stabilized
levels, the layers stop pretending to be layers.

''Prompts:'' which deep polities trade and which raid? What does the Menzoberranzan-shaped hole
in Rhea's past imply about routes from HERE? Where do the whispered House-of-Masks ways come out?

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/outer-seas>>

!! The Outer Seas, Islands & Shores

''Canon:'' the sea-level ring stands ''young'' — towns and ports founded after the flight,
where risen settlements left their harbors behind; each with its own trade goods and Lares
shrines. The partial-lift islands (Mykonos, Naxos, the gradient's middle) carry the strangest
skylines: half a town aloft, half at anchor, lift-traffic between. Wave-jammers skim the crystal harbors; the Astral Sea gnaws
the coastlines; contested Astral waters carry diplomatic traffic and smuggling wars both.
Political intrigue among the Free Cities rides every tide-table. The volcanic Thira-mirror
islands stand in the chain; the flotilla-fresco regatta tradition dresses festival days.

''Prompts:'' name five ports and their one export each. Which island keeps the oldest
First-Breaking cult fragment? Where do the smuggling wars actually land their cargo?

<<~/ahu>>

